      "writtenOn": "2017-03-24T18:03:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking about this a little bit more.  Do we need ENABLE in the config?  I assume when an Alarm is raised, VOLTHA/Adapters can either forward it to Kafka or suppress it.    In my opinion, we should only have SUPPRESS.  When a user wants to suppress a specific alarm, a AlarmConfig(id, SUPPRESS) will be added to the AlarmConfigs.   If the user wants to re-enable that alarm then that entry will be removed from the AlarmConfigs.   The API  \"enableAll\" will clear the config while the \"supressAll\" API will create a wildcard entry AlarmConfig(*, SUPPRESS) in the config.\n\nThoughts?",
      "revId": "5c6d30374e07f62dfc63a9921a5623c87bc45da2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_47e8587c",
        "filename": "voltha/protos/device.proto",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 64,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000127
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-24T19:02:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes we need to have ENABLE option as the operator was asking to have the provision to enable/suppress individual alarms.\nBy default CRITICAL alarms are only enabled as part of adapater bringup. \nThen based on operator/user command specific/all alarms can be enabled/suppressed.",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_e7d76cbe",
      "revId": "5c6d30374e07f62dfc63a9921a5623c87bc45da2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
