      "writtenOn": "2017-03-24T14:55:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How do we change the config for 1 alarm only?  If the device has 1000 alarms in its config and I want to change only 1 of them, how do i do that?",
      "revId": "5c6d30374e07f62dfc63a9921a5623c87bc45da2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_c748e8ce",
        "filename": "voltha/protos/voltha.proto",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000127
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-24T17:42:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assuming the device ID is 123456789, and you would like to SUPPRESS just one Alarm \"Alarm1000\"out of 1000 alarms configured, use this RPC and body should be as below.\n\n{\n  \"id\": \"123456789\",\n  \"alarm_cfg\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"SUPPRESS\",\n      \"name\": \"Alarm1000\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nWhen the simulated adapter gets the update alarm config request, it would take care to just SUPPRESS this alarm of 1000 configured alarms. The 999 other alarms would remain unaffected.\nI have verified such a test case to be working fine.",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_c7c34837",
      "revId": "5c6d30374e07f62dfc63a9921a5623c87bc45da2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_275fa474",
        "filename": "voltha/protos/voltha.proto",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-24T18:03:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the explanation.   So, when updating the alarm configs, if the alarm is present then update it otherwise, add it.  Correct?   How do you handle the case where we need to remove an alarm from the config?  Would this same API be used or you will have another API?",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_c748e8ce",
      "revId": "5c6d30374e07f62dfc63a9921a5623c87bc45da2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_27ed648c",
        "filename": "voltha/protos/voltha.proto",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000127
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-24T19:02:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As per the implementation ONLY alarms which have ENABLE configured are pushed to eventbus and then kafka form there.\nAbsence of any configuration OR SUPPRESS configuration for any alarm means the alarm is suppressed. \nI dont think there is need to remove an Alarm from config to disable it. If there is a need to disable a configured alarm, push a SUPPRESS config for that alarm.",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_275fa474",
      "revId": "5c6d30374e07f62dfc63a9921a5623c87bc45da2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_c7fb4846",
        "filename": "voltha/protos/voltha.proto",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-24T19:22:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So your alarm list is a static list?   If a device gets upgraded with a new set of alarms then the adapter will need to be upgraded (hence voltha) to register this alarm?\n\nThe above logic of updating only 1 alarm does not work as it will overwrite the other 999 alarms in the config.  The code in device_agent just take whatever comes from the API and overwrite the existing data.",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_27ed648c",
      "revId": "5c6d30374e07f62dfc63a9921a5623c87bc45da2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba092121_925eace8",
        "filename": "voltha/protos/voltha.proto",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000127
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-25T18:36:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, in the current design it is assumed that the adapter for a device has a static list of alarms that can be enabled/suppressed. Hence the adapter needs an updated list for any new alarm (or removing an alarm). I guess this is the case for any change in interface between the adapter and the device.\nYou are right in the sense that pushing a config change for a single alarm will overwrite the existing data at the core. The core always stores the latest config. In this specific case of alarm configuration, the voltha core is more so acting like a medium to transfer NB request for alarm configs. The device adapter maintains the entire context of alarms.",
      "parentUuid": "ba092121_c7fb4846",
      "revId": "5c6d30374e07f62dfc63a9921a5623c87bc45da2",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
